# Part of the desktop-container deploy tree (deploy/README.md, "Desktop user
# identity"). Name ONE existing host account here, on a line of its own, and
# the container's "desktop" session user adopts its uid, primary gid and
# password hash at every boot -- so files the desktop writes to shared mounts
# are owned by that host user, and su/sudo inside the container take that
# user's password.
#
#   echo alice > /etc/desktop-container/desktop-user
#   systemctl restart desktop-user-sync.service desktop.service
#
# The account must already exist on the host (this tree never creates it) and
# must not be root. Its NAME is not adopted: the login name inside the
# container stays "desktop" regardless, only the numbers and the password
# follow. A host account literally named "desktop" therefore matches all the
# way through, but nothing requires it.
#
# Empty (the shipped state) = feature off: the container keeps the uid 1000
# baked into the image, exactly as it behaved before this file existed.
